menu "ToDoHelper debug shell"

    config TODOHELPER_DEBUG_SHELL
        bool "Enable the on-device debug shell (/api/v1/debug/exec)"
        default n
        help
            Adds a small text-command shell reachable over HTTP so a developer
            can inspect and drive the device without a serial cable:

                curl -X POST -d 'widgets token' http://<dev>/api/v1/debug/exec
                curl -X POST -d 'click 知道了'   http://<dev>/api/v1/debug/exec

            It can switch pages, press widgets, dump the LVGL object tree, read
            heaps/tasks/NVS and reboot the board. That is exactly why it is
            **off by default** and why its routes always require the HTTP auth
            token even when authentication is otherwise disabled.

            Turn this on for a debugging build only; do not ship it enabled.

endmenu
